      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 15,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 12,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Example Queries for ad hoc log analysis\n### filter\n* `error -exception` all messages containing the [word](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/index.html#word-filter) \"error\", but not \"exception\"\n* `\"[123]: cannot open file\"` exact [phrase filter](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/index.html#phrase-filter)\n* `~\"err|warn\"` substring / [regex filter](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#regexp-filter). case sensitive!\n* `err*`,`'unexpected fail'*` [prefix filter](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#prefix-filter)\n* `i('err*')` [case insentive filtering](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/index.html#case-insensitive-filter), LogsQL supports [quoting](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#string-literals) via double quotes `\"`, single quotes `'` and backticks `\n* `compose_service: gitlab` apply word filter on specific field.\n* `compose_service:~ \"git.+\"` apply regex filter on field\n*  No field specified (above) is just a shortcut for `_msg: <filter>`\n* `| stream_context before 2 after 5` show [context](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#stream_context-pipe) lines before/after matching messages\n\n### extract & format\n* `| extract \"ip=<ip> \"` [extract fields](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#extract-pipe) from message with pattern\n* `| unpack_json` [parse json](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#unpack_json-pipe) from msg to fields\n* `| unpack_logfmt` [parse logfmt](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#unpack_logfmt-pipe) from msg\n* `| format \"request from <ip>:<port>\"` change output [format](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#format-pipe)\n* `| format if (ip:* and host:*) \"request from <ip>:<host>\"` only [reformat line if](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#conditional-format) it contains these fields\n\n* `| unpack_logfmt | status:>300 status:<400` parse log message, then apply [range comparison filter](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victorialogs/logsql/#range-comparison-filter) on extracted field\n\n### Ad Hoc Filtering\n\nClicking a log message shows the available fields, (+) or (-) buttons can be used to quickly add add hoc filters",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.1.1",
      "title": "",
      "type": "text"
    },
